// Formula: [Role] + [Tech Stack] + [Differentiator] + [Value]

// Example 1: Focus on learning speed
"I'm a Java backend developer skilled in Spring Boot and PostgreSQL who learns
new technologies fast—I went from zero Docker knowledge to containerizing and
deploying a microservices project in two weeks."

// Example 2: Focus on code quality
"I'm a Java backend developer with strong Spring Boot fundamentals who writes
well-tested, maintainable code—my internship API had 85% test coverage and zero
production bugs in its first three months."

// Example 3: Focus on problem-solving
"I'm a Java backend developer experienced in building REST APIs with Spring Boot,
known for debugging complex issues—I once traced a race condition through three
microservices to find a database locking problem."

// Example 4: Focus on specific domain
"I'm a Java backend developer specializing in Spring Boot and SQL who built
a complete e-commerce backend handling orders, inventory, and payments with
transaction safety."

// BAD Example: Buzzword-heavy, no substance
"I'm a passionate, dynamic full-stack engineer leveraging cutting-edge
technologies to deliver innovative solutions with exceptional teamwork skills."
// ^ Says nothing specific, applies to anyone, instantly forgettable

// STRONG: Specific technical delivery
"Delivered three production-ready REST APIs using Spring Boot, each handling
authentication, data validation, error handling, and comprehensive unit tests—
with zero critical bugs reported in the first six months."
// Why it works: Specific, quantified, demonstrates competence and reliability

// STRONG: Problem-solving with evidence
"Debugs complex issues systematically—traced a production race condition through
three microservices to identify a database locking problem that had stumped
the team for weeks."
// Why it works: Shows advanced debugging skills with a concrete example

// STRONG: Learning velocity
"Fast learner who goes from tutorial to production—picked up Spring Boot from
zero knowledge and built a deployed e-commerce backend within two months,
including payment integration and order processing."
// Why it works: Demonstrates ability to learn and apply quickly with specifics

// WEAK: Generic trait
"Hardworking and passionate about technology"
// Why it fails: Applies to everyone, no evidence, not differentiating

// WEAK: Aspirational, not proven
"Wants to become a full-stack developer and learn cloud technologies"
// Why it fails: Future-focused, doesn't show what you've already delivered
